We now test our approach on two sets of breast cancer data, namely:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Breast cancer diagnosis from Wisconsin dataset~\cite{UCI_Wisconsin_Breast_Cancer} with two classification labels (benign and malignant);
    \item Brest cancer classification from the Molecular Taxonomy of Breast Cancer International Consortium (METABRIC)~\cite{METABRIC_Kaggle}. We used the patient's vital status (alive, died of the disease, and died of other causes) for the classification labels. 
