After a warm-up of 200 time steps, the model was trained on 1600 time steps to learn the Lorenz-63 dynamics accurately. It was then evaluated on a 200-time step test set. As mentioned in the theoretical explanation of the model, the adaptive NVAR model learns the increment $\Delta X_i = X_{i+1} - X_i$, rather than directly predicting the next state $X_{i+1}$.

For the noisy cases, we applied a 10\% dropout rate to the same shallow MLP architecture and the delay parameter was increased to \( k = 30 \).


