In healthcare, digital twins enable personalized and proactive treatment by digitally replicating patient physiology~\cite{erol2020digital, ankitha2024healthcare}. Numerous smart healthcare applications have emerged, such as CloudDTH, which monitors, diagnoses, and predicts elderly health using wearable IoT devices~\cite{liu2019novel}, and a smart home healthcare that detects atrial fibrillation and falls using ECG and WiFi signals~\cite{chen2023digital}. Thiong’o~\el proposed a DT to predict neurological complications in pediatric cancer patients by interfacing AI with patient-specific cancer profiles~\cite{thiong2022digital}. Another application is found in virtual medical training~\cite{haleem2023exploring}. Ultimately, it enhances patient outcomes and overall quality of life.

