We also observe that increasing the value of $p$ in the generalized objective improves the performance of both \textsc{FW} and \textsc{MNP}, whereas \textsc{SuperGreedy++} remains largely unaffected. In fact, for all values of $p$ considered, both \textsc{FW} and \textsc{MNP} show improved performance compared to the classical Densest Subgraph case ($p = 1$).

