    \textbf{Limitation.} Although introducing ILVC does not significantly increase the overhead during training, there are still some costs associated with inference. For QA or caption tasks, if mask decoding is not required, the inference efficiency of these tasks will not be affected. For more complex tasks such as Grounded Conversational Generation, there is an additional inference overhead of approximately 15\%. Our proposed method achieves a top-1 accuracy of 25.7\% for logits in AttrEval and 58.6\% in question answering, indicating considerable room for improvement in attribute inference. These results highlight the need for further exploration to enhance semantic understanding and alignment capabilities in the future.

