acts on the quantum register and the qubit presently scanned by the quantum work tape head. %\footnote{In Watrous' original definition \cite{W03} of this QTM model, the quantum transitions depend only on the current state $q$ of the machine. The version we use here is equivalent in power (each step of our machines can be simulated in two steps by Watrous' machines), and is preferred because its specialization to the formal definition of the 2QCFA model \cite{AW02} (to be introduced shortly) is trivial.} 
