Our constructions in Sections \ref{sec:hier1} and \ref{sec:hier2} involve various subroutines that are obtained by adapting two basic 2QCFA algorithms. The first of these recognizes the language \orderedeq{} in polynomial expected time, and was discovered by Remscrim \cite{R20}.\footnote{Ambainis and Watrous were the first to present a polynomial-time 2QCFA for \orderedeq{} in \cite{AW02}, but their algorithm uses some amplitudes  that are not restricted to being algebraic, and thus does not fit our QTM definition.}
