    \item Any two segments separated by a $\$$ belong in different blocks, so the segment on the right should be one symbol longer than the one on the right. The \textsc{SameLength} procedure is employed to check this condition by comparing the number of symbol occurrences in the left segment with the length of a sequence defined to consist of the $\$$ separator \textit{and} all the symbols of the right segment in stage (C2).
