    \label{fig:ablation_gnn}
\end{figure}



\subsubsection{Multi-Head Attention Module} 
A comprehensive ablation study was performed on the different sub-modules of the attention based fusion mechanism for allowing the model to focus on the specific parts of the structure aware and context aware embeddings. We observe that using a multi-head attention method considerably improves the performance. Using a layer-norm to normalize the layer outputs increases the stability of the training and helps the model converge. For small datasets, including dropout prevents overfitting and helps the model generalize better. Interestingly, including a residual layer does not lead to a significant improvement in model performance.The waterfall chart\ref{fig:ablation_attn} captures the effect of each change on the model performance.

