\section{Conclusion}
\vspace{-3pt}
In this study, we propose to derive linguistic constraints from pre-trained language models and speech-language models to optimize AV-TSE. Evaluated on multilingual, visual cue-impaired, and cross-domain test sets, the proposed paradigm consistently outperforms the vanilla AV-TSE backbone, while the linguistic constraints from the language model surpass those of the speech model.  
In future work, we aim to explore other methods of injecting language information and semantics to further improve AV-TSE performance.

