\subsection{Generator}
Based on the characteristics of each \textit{focal method} in the benchmark test set and its \textit{NLD of method's intention}, we extended the basic prompt template originally used in ChatTester by incorporating the \textit{NLD of method's intention}. The resulting prompt includes the method signature, method body, \textit{NLD of method's intention}, and contextual information such as class definitions, related method signatures, relevant fields, and import statements to construct a structured input. The LLM is then guided to generate \textit{candidate test cases} for the defective \textit{focal method}.

\subsection{Validator}
Test case repair is a commonly used module owing to its verified effectiveness \cite{b57}. Therefore, we inherit the \textit{Validator} of \textsc{ChatTester} \cite{b22} with compile and error repair phases in DISTINCT. Specifically, \textit{Validator} first performs a compilation check on the \textit{candidate test cases}. If the compilation succeeds, the process continues to subsequent analysis steps; if the compilation fails, an iterative repair strategy is employed to revise the \textit{candidate test cases} with both error messages and details provided. These error messages typically include the error type (such as missing dependency errors, unresolved method or symbol errors, unimplemented abstract class errors, and method override errors) and error details (e.g., the exact line number and the specific method signature involved).
