This repair process is performed iteratively. If \textit{candidate test cases} continue to fail compilation after a repair attempt, the \textit{Validator} re-extracts the latest error messages and triggers another repair iteration. This loop continues until the test case compiles successfully or the number of iterations reaches the predefined upper limit, \textit{Max Iteration-Val = 5}.

