\subsubsection{Candidate Test Case Analysis}
In this stage, we perform logic analysis on the compilation-passed \textit{candidate test case} to extract all the logic branches exercised by the test cases, referred to as the \textit{test case logic branch}. To guide this analysis, we construct the following prompt: ``\textit{You are a Java logic analysis expert. Given the test cases, list all logic branches exercised by the test cases, including conditionals, loops, and exceptions. Focus only on the branches actually triggered during execution.}'' This prompt directs the LLM to identify only the branches that are actively covered by the execution of the \textit{candidate test case}. As illustrated in Figure~\ref{fig:example2}, the LLM infers all the logical branches triggered by the candidate test case based on the focal method.

