\section{Evaluation Result}
\subsection{RQ2: How do DISTINT perform against SOTA methods?}

Table \textrm{I} shows that ChatTester with NLD and ChatTester without NLD have similar CSRs, with the former at 24.59\%—representing a 7.15\% improvement over the latter. However, the PR of unit tests generated by ChatTester with NLD on repaired methods reaches 13.93\%, representing a 324\% improvement over ChatTester without NLD. This indicates that an accurate NLD of the focal method helps the LLM understand the true intent of the defective method, rather than inferring potentially incorrect intent from the code itself. Consequently, the model generates unit tests that better align with the repaired method, achieving a higher passing rate on repaired methods.

Table \textrm{I} demonstrates that ChatTester with NLD achieves a line coverage of 71.27\%, comparable to EvoSuite and representing a 10.33\% improvement over ChatTester without NLD, its BC is 79.13\%, nearly on par with ChatTester without NLD and slightly below EvoSuite. However, a notable improvement is observed after providing the NLD to the LLM: ChatTester’s DDR increases from 0\% (without NLD) to 1.36\%. This strongly suggests that introducing the NLD positively enhances the task of generating unit tests for defective methods, offering substantial research and improvement potential.

ChatUniTest with NLD outperforms its variant without NLD in both CSR and test passing rate, demonstrating the effectiveness of the NLD mechanism (achieving relative improvements of 20.01\% and 95.81\% on Defects4J, 0.0\% and 15.0\% on QuixBugs when NLD is used). ChatUniTest’s DDR increases from 0\% (without NLD) to 1.36\%, and its BC and SC improve by 24.36\% and 15.24\%, respectively, indicating enhanced reliability and test utility. However, like the others, it also fails to generate any defect-revealing test cases.

Compared to the SOTA, our approach DISTINCT achieves notable improvements across all metrics on both Defects4J-Desc and QuixBugs-Desc in the non-regression testing scenario. Specifically, it improves CSRs by 19.6\% and 9.68\%, test passing rates by 9.32\% and 4.17\%, and DDR by 149.26\% and 41.18\%, respectively. It also enhances BC by 6.34\% and 4.37\%, and SC by 2.07\% and 5.48\%, demonstrating its superior effectiveness and robustness across benchmarks.

