\subsection{RQ4: Can DISTINCT maintain high coverage and DDR across different LLMs?}


Table \textrm{III} demonstrates that DISTINCT consistently improves test generation performance across a variety of state-of-the-art LLMs, including both general-purpose and code-specific models, confirming its strong generality and adaptability.

With the original base model DeepSeek, DISTINCT substantially improves all metrics and performs better than all other LLMs. The CSR increases from 22.40\% to 29.48\% (31.61\% relative improvement), and the PR rises from 10.18\% to 15.84\% (55.60\% increase). Most notably, DDR improves from 2.04\% to 3.39\% (66.18\% boost). Code coverage also improves significantly, with BC rising by 11.27\% (from 66.70\% to 74.20\%) and SC by 14.10\% (from 66.70\% to 81.40\%).

The generality of DISTINCT is further validated across LLaMA3-70B, LLaMA3-8B, and CodeLLaMA-7B. While the base models struggle with CSR and DDR, DISTINCT consistently enhances all metrics. Because Llama3-8B is a small-parameter model, it performs worse than medium-parameter models like Llama3-70B and code-specific models like CodeLlama-7B in areas such as handling complex logic, processing long-context code, and understanding programming languages. As a result, Llama3-8B performs worse than all other LLMs on basic prompts. However, on DISTINCT, its CSR increased by 222.35\%, PR improved by 86.89\%, DDR rose from 0\% to 2.95\%, and its coverage also saw a significant improvement.Llama3-70B and CodeLlama-7B both show substantial gains on DISTINCT compared to basic prompts. Specifically, Llama3-70B achieved a 153.1\% increase in CSP, a 77.38\% improvement in PR, and its DDR rose from 0\% to 3.17\%. CodeLlama-7B followed with a 97.84\% increase in CSP, a 91.73\% improvement in PR, and an impressive 555.6\% boost in DDR. Both models also saw significant improvements in coverage. These results highlight that medium-parameter and code-specific models outperform small models in tasks involving complex logic and test case generation—though they still fall short compared to the large-parameter DeepSeek-V3.

in most cases—demonstrating DISTINCT’s robustness regardless of LLM architecture or size.

These improvements across diverse LLMs can be attributed to DISTINCT’s model-agnostic design. By introducing structured components such as the Analyzer, which extracts logic branches from the code, and the Validator, which filters and refines test cases based on execution signals, DISTINCT provides external guidance that mitigates the limitations of weaker or smaller LLMs. This design effectively decouples test quality from the raw capabilities of the underlying language model, enabling DISTINCT to maintain high levels of DDR and code coverage regardless of the backbone model.


