\subsection{Blocking Pairs}
\label{sec:bp}

A nice link between almost stable matchings and stable partition properties was made by \textcite{abraham06}. They provided bounds on the minimum number of blocking pairs admitted by any matching of a given {\sc sr} instance in terms of its invariant odd cycles. Precisely, for an {\sc sr} instance $I$, let $\mathcal{C}$ denote the collection of cycles of odd length at least three in a stable partition of $I$, then $\left\lceil \frac{\vert \mathcal{C}\vert}{2} \right\rceil \leq bp(I)\leq \vert\mathcal{C}\vert(n -2)$ (adapted to the case of complete preference lists).

