\begin{definition}[Monotonicity]\label{def:mono}
For set $Q$, a set function $f:2^{Q}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is monotone non-decreasing (or non-increasing) if $f(H) \leq f(T)$ (or $f(H) \geq f(T)$) holds for all $H \subseteq T \subseteq Q$.
