\begin{definition}[Submodularity]\label{def:sub}
A set function $f:2^{Q}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is said to be submodular if
\begin{equation*}\label{submod}
f(H \cup \{u\}) - f(H) \geq f(T\cup \{u\}) - f(T)
\end{equation*}
