Given any positive integer $k$ and an error parameter $\epsilon \in (0,1)$, the run-time of Algorithm~\ref{alg:fastgrad} is $\tilde{O}(km \hat{l}/\epsilon^2)$. Through the iterative selection of $k$ edges, the algorithm produces a solution $T$. Furthermore, the gradient of the edge selected in each round constitutes an $\epsilon$-approximation of the maximal gradient of the objective function.
